<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="67742" href="schedule/2022/spring/BIOE/198/67742.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120221" href="schedule/2022/spring.xml">Spring 2022</term><subject id="BIOE" href="schedule/2022/spring/BIOE.xml">Bioengineering</subject><course id="198" href="schedule/2022/spring/BIOE/198.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>MI </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Biomedical Data Analysis</sectionTitle><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This computational laboratory experience introduces students to formatting, analysis, and visualization of biomedical data. Based in Matlab, students learn to read data from instruments and to simulate data using numerical models in one or several dimensions. Statistical methods are introduced for managing stochastic data at various scales. The objective is to gain experience solving fundamental engineering problems that focus on medical and biological applications.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-01-18Z</startDate><endDate>2022-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>3117</roomNumber><buildingName>Everitt Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Babaei" firstName="S">Babaei, S</instructor><instructor lastName="Insana" firstName="M">Insana, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Newman" firstName="W">Newman, W</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>